    "alert_id": "TDF_PHOSPHATE_LOW",
    "title": "Low phosphate with TDF suggests tubular toxicity",
    "message": "Guidelines list renal failure and tubular wasting syndrome as TDF adverse effects, and recommend eGFR monitoring at 3, 6, then 6–12 monthly intervals, with closer monitoring in high-risk patients including those with co-existent hypertension. Patient has serum phosphate 0.78 mmol/L and trace proteinuria on TDF for 6 years with hypertension. TDF can cause proximal tubular dysfunction leading to phosphate wasting and proteinuria. Against drug attribution: trace proteinuria may stem from uncontrolled hypertension, and phosphate was measured only once without baseline comparison. However, the combination of low phosphate, proteinuria, and TDF exposure warrants evaluation for tubulopathy.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Check eGFR, urinary phosphate, and consider renal tubular function assessment. If tubulopathy confirmed, consider switching TDF to TAF or alternative NRTI.",
