    "alert_id": "TDF_IBUPROFEN_NEPHROTOXICITY",
    "title": "TDF plus NSAID increases renal risk",
    "message": "Guidelines note TDF can cause renal failure and recommend eGFR monitoring, especially in high-risk patients with co-existent hypertension. Patient takes PRN ibuprofen alongside TDF and has hypertension with BP 146/94 and trace proteinuria today. Concurrent TDF and NSAID use compounds nephrotoxic risk through additive effects on renal tubular and haemodynamic function. The clinician's plan continues both TDF and PRN ibuprofen without flagging this interaction. Creatinine of 112 umol/L is within normal limits but represents a single snapshot; no trend data are available.",
    "issue_type": "drug_interaction",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Counsel patient to minimise ibuprofen use; consider alternative analgesia. Monitor renal function more frequently given combined nephrotoxic risk.",
