    "alert_id": "TDF_EGFR_MONITORING_GAP",
    "title": "eGFR not documented despite TDF risk factors",
    "message": "Guidelines require eGFR monitoring at 3 months, 6 months, then 6–12 monthly on TDF, with additional monitoring in high-risk patients including those with hypertension. Patient has been on TDF for 6 years and has hypertension, yet only serum creatinine is reported today without eGFR calculation. Trace proteinuria and low phosphate further elevate renal risk. The clinician's plan does not include eGFR assessment or enhanced renal monitoring. Creatinine alone may underestimate renal impairment, particularly in this higher-risk patient.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Calculate eGFR from today's creatinine. Given hypertension and proteinuria, schedule renal monitoring at least every 6 months including eGFR and urinalysis.",
