    "alert_id": "EFV_LONGTERM_USE",
    "title": "EFV after 6 years: consider neuropsychiatric review",
    "message": "Guidelines list EFV as a current regimen component but do not explicitly address long-term EFV continuation thresholds. Patient has been on EFV for 6 years with viral suppression and CD4 of 540. He reports a heavy feeling in both thighs and stiff gait, which could reflect chronic EFV neuropsychiatric effects or peripheral neuropathy. Against drug attribution: symptoms are also consistent with occupational musculoskeletal strain from truck driving. No baseline neurological findings are documented for comparison. Many guidelines now prefer dolutegravir-based regimens over EFV for tolerability.",
    "issue_type": "medication_safety",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Assess for EFV-related neuropsychiatric symptoms and peripheral neuropathy. Consider regimen review for potential switch to a better-tolerated ARV.",
