  {
    "alert_id": "PROTEINURIA_HYPERTENSION_TDF",
    "title": "Trace proteinuria needs workup beyond hypertension",
    "message": "Guidelines identify TDF as a cause of tubular wasting syndrome and renal failure, and recommend enhanced monitoring in high-risk patients with hypertension. Patient has trace proteinuria attributed solely to hypertension in the plan, but TDF-related tubular dysfunction is an alternative or contributing cause, especially given low phosphate. The plan does not include quantitative protein assessment or renal tubular evaluation. Distinguishing hypertensive nephropathy from TDF tubulopathy requires further investigation, as management differs significantly.",
    "issue_type": "plan_review",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Order urine protein-to-creatinine ratio and renal tubular markers. If TDF tubulopathy suspected, consider switching to TAF or alternative.",
